course: dictionary
lesson: 10003
title: Tell: many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tell is a small word with many jobs. Its most common job is to say something so someone knows it: «Older children in big families often help a lot, but if it gets too much, tell a parent or a teacher.» Here tell means say it so they know.
explain: Tell can also mean to see or know a difference, as in «I can't tell the twins apart.» Or it can mean to read a clock, as in tell the time. The words around tell show which meaning you need.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping in your idea. «If Gran says "keep the change", telling her how much is left makes it an honest gift.» Does say fit here? Yes, because telling her means saying how much is left, so she knows.
explain: Tell can also be a noun in games, where a tell is a sign that gives you away. Tell, tells, told and telling are all forms of the same verb, so check which one fits the sentence.
fact: Tell is a verb: tell, tells, told, telling.
fact: «Tell» can mean to say something so that someone knows it.
fact: «Tell apart» means to see the difference between two things.
fact: «Tell the time» means to read a clock.
fact: «Tell on someone» means to report them to a grown-up. In a game, a tell is a sign that gives you away.
exercise: «If it gets too much, tell a parent or a teacher.» What does tell mean here? | Count the words aloud | Stay quiet about it | *Say it so they know | Read a clock
exercise: «I can't tell the twins apart.» What does tell apart mean? | Hide them from each other | *See the difference between them | Tell them a joke | Give them a prize
exercise: Which word is the past form of tell? | Telling | Tell | Tells | *Told
test: In casual talk, «tell me about it» means what? | Tell me the time | I am lost | Please tell me a story | *I agree, it's true
test: «If someone tells you a hurtful thing another person said, check with that person directly.» What should you do? | Say nothing ever | *Check with that person directly | Repeat it to everyone | Tell it as a joke
exam: Which meaning fits tell as a noun? | A story said out loud | *A sign that gives you away, in games | To read a clock | To order someone to do something
